    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d477">

                <pb facs="0821" n="751" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg751"/>

                <head>No. 478.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee
                        to Mr. Bátres.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 11,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have had the honor to receive your note
                    of the 24th ultimo, and have had a copy of it and other papers at the
                    Department, in relation to the schooner Ounalaska, forwarded to the
                    Attorney-General of the United States for such use as may be deemed advisable in
                    any prosecution against that vessel at San Francisco, whither she has been
                    dispatched, under guard, by the United States minister to the Central American
                    States, for having violated the neutrality laws of this country.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ALVEY A. ADEE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
